        "en" to GemDetails(
            "Chondrodite is a fluorinated magnesium silicate of the humite group, related to olivine. It mainly forms in contact marbles, when a fluorine-rich granitic intrusion metamorphoses dolomitic limestones: magnesium from the dolomite combines with silica and fluorine brought by magmatic fluids. It is also found in some carbonatites and skarns. Its orange to reddish-brown crystals, usually small, are hard to tell apart by eye from clinohumite, its close cousin.",
